---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import '../styles/legal.css';
import { site, pending } from '../data/site';
import { withBase } from '../utils/url';

/* Was a show/hide flag during design iteration; production always shows it. */
const showContents = true;

const contents = [
  { id: 'collect', label: 'What I collect' },
  { id: 'cookies', label: 'Cookies and analytics' },
  { id: 'inquiry-form', label: 'The inquiry form' },
  { id: 'keep', label: 'How long I keep it' },
  { id: 'clients', label: 'Client records are different' },
  { id: 'requests', label: 'Your requests' },
  { id: 'terms', label: 'Terms of use' },
];
---

<Base
  title="Site policies"
  description="How this website handles your information, and the terms on which you use it."
  chrome="legal"
  legalSibling={{ label: 'Tax advice notice', href: '/tax-advice-notice' }}
>
  <div class="container legal">
    <h1 class="h1 legal__title">Site policies</h1>
    {/* Page opener: the one horizontal gold rule on this page. */}
    <hr class="gold-rule legal__rule" />
    <p class="lead measure-64 legal__intro">
      How this website handles your information, and the terms on which you use it. Two sections:
      privacy first, then terms of use.
    </p>
    <p class="label legal__effective">EFFECTIVE {pending.legalEffectiveDate}</p>
    <p class="confirm-note measure-64 legal__draft">
      Draft for your review. I am not a lawyer and this text has not been reviewed by one — the
      bracketed notes mark the points that need your confirmation or an attorney's eye before this
      page goes live.
    </p>

    {
      showContents && (
        <nav aria-label="On this page" class="toc">
          <p class="label label--strong toc__label">ON THIS PAGE</p>
          <div class="toc__links">
            {contents.map((entry) => (
              <a href={`#${entry.id}`}>{entry.label}</a>
            ))}
          </div>
        </nav>
      )
    }

    <div class="legal__body">
      <section id="collect">
        <h2 class="h2 legal__h2">What I collect</h2>
        <p class="legal__p">
          Two things, and nothing else. First, basic traffic measurement — which pages were viewed,
          when, roughly where the visit came from, and what kind of device it was. Second, whatever
          you choose to type into the inquiry form.
        </p>
        <p class="legal__p">
          I do not sell information, share it with advertisers, or add anyone to a mailing list.
          There is no advertising on this site and no third-party tracking beyond the analytics
          described below.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="cookies">
        <h2 class="h2 legal__h2">Cookies and analytics</h2>
        <p class="legal__p">
          This site uses Google Analytics to count visits and see which pages get read. Google
          Analytics sets cookies in your browser — small files that let it recognise a returning
          visit. That data goes to Google and is subject to Google's own privacy terms.
        </p>
        <p class="legal__p">
          You can refuse or delete these cookies in your browser settings, or install Google's
          opt-out browser add-on. Nothing on this site stops working if you do.
        </p>
        <p class="confirm-note">
          [CONFIRM] Whether IP anonymisation is switched on in your Analytics property, and whether
          you want a cookie consent banner. This site currently discloses cookies in the footer
          rather than asking for consent — appropriate for a US-only audience, but not sufficient if
          you expect visitors in the EU or UK.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="inquiry-form">
        <h2 class="h2 legal__h2">The inquiry form</h2>
        <p class="legal__p">
          The form asks for a name, an email address, and a message. When you send it, that becomes
          an email to me. It is not stored in a database on this website, and no one else receives a
          copy.
        </p>
        <p class="legal__p">
          Please don't put Social Security numbers, account numbers, or tax documents in a first
          message. Ordinary email is not a secure channel; once you're a client, I'll tell you how to
          send documents properly.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="keep">
        <h2 class="h2 legal__h2">How long I keep it</h2>
        <p class="legal__p">
          Inquiry emails stay in my mail account while a conversation is live and for a reasonable
          period afterwards. Analytics data is retained on the schedule set in the Analytics
          property.
        </p>
        <p class="confirm-note">
          [CONFIRM] A stated retention period — for example, inquiry emails deleted after 12 months
          if no engagement follows, and Analytics set to 14 months. Naming a period is better than "a
          reasonable period."
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="clients">
        <h2 class="h2 legal__h2">Client records are different</h2>
        <p class="legal__p">
          This page is about the website. Tax documents, books, and anything else you give me as a
          client are handled under your engagement letter and the confidentiality rules that apply to
          a CPA — not under this notice. Those obligations are stricter, and they continue after an
          engagement ends.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="requests">
        <h2 class="h2 legal__h2">Your requests</h2>
        <p class="legal__p">
          Write to <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> to ask what I hold about you, to
          correct it, or to have it deleted. I'll answer myself.
        </p>
        <p class="confirm-note">
          [CONFIRM] Whether any state privacy statute applies to the practice — this depends on
          client residency and revenue thresholds, and it's the clause most worth an attorney's five
          minutes.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="terms" class="legal__terms">
        <h2 class="h2 legal__h2">Terms of use</h2>
        <p class="legal__p legal__p--spaced">
          By using this site you accept the following. It is short on purpose.
        </p>

        <div class="subsections">
          <div>
            <h3 class="h3 legal__h3">This site is information, not advice</h3>
            <p class="legal__p">
              Everything here describes services in general terms. None of it is tax, accounting, or
              regulatory advice for your situation, and reading it does not make you a client. The
              <a href={withBase('/tax-advice-notice')}>tax advice notice</a> covers this in full.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="h3 legal__h3">Accuracy</h3>
            <p class="legal__p">
              I keep this site current, but tax law changes constantly and pages can fall behind.
              Nothing here is warranted to be complete or up to date on the day you read it.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="h3 legal__h3">Links out</h3>
            <p class="legal__p">
              Where this site links to the IRS, FINRA, or anyone else, that is a convenience. I don't
              control those sites and a link is not an endorsement.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="h3 legal__h3">The content itself</h3>
            <p class="legal__p">
              The text, marks, and design of this site belong to {site.name}. You're welcome to quote
              a sentence with attribution; please don't republish pages wholesale.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="h3 legal__h3">Changes</h3>
            <p class="legal__p">
              These policies can change. The effective date at the top tells you which version you're
              reading.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="h3 legal__h3">Governing law</h3>
            <p class="legal__p legal__p--spaced">
              These terms are governed by the law of {pending.governingLawState}.
            </p>
            <p class="confirm-note">
              [CONFIRM] The state, and whether you want a limitation-of-liability clause here. I've
              deliberately left one out rather than draft it unreviewed.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="legal__questions">
        <h2 class="h2 legal__h2 legal__h2--sm">Questions about any of this</h2>
        <p class="legal__p">
          Call <a href={site.phoneHref}>{site.phone}</a> or write to
          <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
